tool-call syntax. Do not quote or place tool-call markup inside explanatory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 49 actions; a strong score needs about 39 or fewer. You are 1.3x over the target.\nIf you are not steadily making progress toward the level goal, commit to your single best hypothesis and the shortest sequence that tests it \u2014 do not exhaustively scan rows/columns or enumerate every option. Test one idea, read the result, then decide.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "Neither alignment worked. I'm at 49 actions and the timer is running very low. Let me think about what I haven't tried:\n1. Maybe the goal involves the yellow platforms - move the blue bar to be above one of them\n2. Maybe the goal is to move the blue bar to the far left or far right edge\n3. Maybe I need to use MOUSE on the yellow platforms\n4. Maybe the goal is to move the blue bar to a specific row\nLet me try a completely different approach. Maybe the goal is to move the blue bar to be centered above the LEFT yellow platform. The left platform is at cols 16-27. The blue bar is 20 cols wide. For the blue bar to be centered above the left platform:\n- Left platform center: col 21.5\n- Blue bar center: col 21.5 \u2192 cols 12-31 (this is the starting position!)\nSo the starting position already has the blue bar centered above the left platform. That's not it.\nWhat about the right platform? Right platform at cols 40-51, center 45.5. Blue bar centered at 45.5 \u2192 cols 36-55. I already tried that (RIGHT 2 from cols 28-47 \u2192 cols 36-55), and it didn't work.\nLet me try moving the blue bar to the far left edge. From cols 20-39, LEFT 5 \u2192 cols 0-19. Or to the far right edge, RIGHT 2 \u2192 cols 40